# width: 120
# `ui.dock.plus_at` (src/app/launcher_dock.zig): which END of the strip
# the `+` takes. `.right` is the shipped look — the `+` is the LAST item,
# after the terminals, right before the pin chip — because a `+` that
# led the run read as odd ("plus on the left feels weird, right side more
# natural"); `.left` is the strip's original shape, the `+` leading.
#
# `:dock end` is the proof's anchor: it butts the run against the pin
# chip, so whatever else is on the strip, the last item is the one
# painted right before `󰐃`. A `contains` check needs no column then.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex dock always
ex dock end
expect screen contains "󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New  󰐃"
# Under `.label` — the word form — the `+` is a character of its word,
# and still the last word on the strip.
ex dock text
expect screen contains "New terminal  + New  󰐃"
ex dock labels
# `:dock plus left` moves it to the head. `:dock start` is that end's
# anchor — the strip's first cell — so the `+` is the first thing on it.
ex dock plus left
expect screen contains "dock: the + at the left end"
ex dock start
expect screen contains "\n  󰐕 New   Browser  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal "
# And back: the same run, the `+` behind it again.
ex dock plus right
expect screen contains "dock: the + at the right end"
expect screen contains "\n   Browser  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New "
ex dock center
# The strip's own menu lists both ends, the live one ticked, in the
# bottom strip's words; and the three running marks, the same idiom.
rightclick 118 37
expect screen contains "✓ + at the right end"
expect screen contains "+ at the left end"
expect screen lacks "✓ + at the left end"
expect screen contains "✓ Running mark: bright icon"
expect screen contains "Running mark: small dot"
expect screen contains "Running mark: none"
key esc
# The Settings rows read the live keys: `[right]` and `[bright]` out of
# the box. Typing narrows the list to the rows that say the word.
command view.settings
type "dock +"
expect screen contains "Launcher dock + end"
expect screen contains "[right]"
key esc
command view.settings
type "running"
expect screen contains "Launcher dock running mark"
expect screen contains "[bright]"
key esc
